🚽 Test case: a zero-argument slorp() passed to a test-only native's
🚽 STDROT_PTR parameter (peek_int, tests/stdrot/testptr.c) is an
🚽 unsupported contextual type -- propagate_contextual_call_type() never
🚽 even attempts it (STDROT_PTR has no single concrete VarType to give
🚽 it) -- and must produce exactly one clear diagnostic, not a second,
🚽 misleading "expected a pointer" error from semantic_check_native_
🚽 call()'s own STDROT_PTR argument check (issue #229). Requires
🚽 STDROT_LIB_PATH pointed at tests/libstdrot.so.
skibidi main {
    peek_int(slorp());
    bussin 0;
}
